0.10 0.14 0.20 rg
BT /F2 22 Tf 44 706 Td (07 / CHOOSE AN AI ARCHITECTURE) Tj ET
0.83 0.90 0.98 RG 44 691 m 568 691 l S
BT /F1 11 Tf 0.19 0.26 0.34 rg 48 667 Td (RULE-BASED: Best when the logic is fixed and does not need a language model.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 0.19 0.26 0.34 rg 48 640 Td (LLM ASSISTANT: Useful for explanation, summarisation and flexible language.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 0.19 0.26 0.34 rg 48 613 Td (RETRIEVAL + LLM: Useful when answers should refer to a verified knowledge base.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 0.19 0.26 0.34 rg 48 586 Td (TOOL-USING AGENT: Suitable when a model chooses among approved read or action) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 0.19 0.26 0.34 rg 48 559 Td (tools, while respecting confirmations and real tool responses.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 0.19 0.26 0.34 rg 48 532 Td (A complex multi-agent design is not automatically better than one clear flow.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 0.19 0.26 0.34 rg 48 505 Td (Use deterministic code for amounts, totals, taxes and eligibility calculations.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 0.19 0.26 0.34 rg 48 478 Td (Only give the model the permissions required for the task.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 0.19 0.26 0.34 rg 48 451 Td (External actions should be visible, reversible where possible and confirmed.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 0.19 0.26 0.34 rg 48 424 Td (Run tests against hallucinations and misleading simulated completions.) Tj ET
