BT /F2 11 Tf 0.039 0.400 0.761 rg 48 667 Td (OPTION A: Cascaded pipeline. Microphone -> speech-to-text -> LLM -> text-to-speech.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 0.19 0.26 0.34 rg 48 640 Td (Advantages: Easy component swapping and visible transcripts for debugging.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 0.19 0.26 0.34 rg 48 613 Td (Trade-offs: Multiple stages can add latency and recognition errors.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 0.039 0.400 0.761 rg 48 586 Td (OPTION B: Realtime speech-to-speech models.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 0.19 0.26 0.34 rg 48 559 Td (Advantages: Natural timing, interruptions and conversational audio in one model.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 0.19 0.26 0.34 rg 48 532 Td (Trade-offs: Availability, pricing and platform constraints vary by provider.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 0.19 0.26 0.34 rg 48 505 Td (For Tamil and English, test natural code-switching and pronunciation.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 0.19 0.26 0.34 rg 48 478 Td (Measure response latency, background noise handling and interruption recovery.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 0.19 0.26 0.34 rg 48 451 Td (Confirm important names, prices and external actions aloud.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 0.19 0.26 0.34 rg 48 424 Td (Offer text input or a human handoff when audio fails.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 0.19 0.26 0.34 rg 48 397 Td (Free voice frameworks do not guarantee free telephony or deployment.) Tj ET
